I posted progress comments on #1002 and #982 and left both open. I didn't comment on any of the other issues.

#1002, `.yoyo/memory.json` now respects `--deny-dir`/`--allow-dir` (`2a7c07f5`)
• **Before and after:** with `memory.json` symlinked into a denied directory, its content still reached the system prompt (1 hit, no warning). Now it's 0 hits plus a ⚠ warning. Targets outside the --allow-dir list are now refused the same way, and with no fence nothing changes.
• **How:** the memory read uses the same check the instruction files got in cf8ad734, not a second helper.
• **Tests:** the new tests pass. With the check neutered, exactly the two refusal tests failed by name.
• **`/spawn:** I checked commands_spawn.rs:510` and it goes through the same fenced loader, so it's covered too. That item is no longer unprobed.
• **Why it stays open:**
  • Skills directories are still unprobed. --print-system-prompt can't show them, so probing them needs a different check.
  • Whether `--safe-mode` should skip the goal file is still a decision for you to make.

#982, `yoyo find` no longer reports success after skipping part of the tree (`995d1c4f`)
• **Before:** a directory it couldn't read was dropped silently. With a chmod-000 subdirectory, yoyo find target_zz printed 1 file matching and exited 0.
• **Now:**
  • It names the unreadable directories on stderr and exits 1, which is how find(1) behaves.
  • Readable trees, no-match results and the git-backed path give the same output as before.
  • A clean search that finds nothing still exits 0, so the open no-match decision is untouched.
• **Why it stays open:** `def`/`outline` not-found, bare `run` and `tree <bad arg>` still exit 0 on failure. Whether `find`/`grep` should exit 1 on no match is also still undecided.

